div_euclid` | `v2 == 0 && v1 == 0` | returns `0` | `e2_zero_over_zero` |\n| E3 | `div_euclid` | `v2 == 0 && v1 == INT_MIN` (rejection wins over the `INT_MIN` guards) | returns `0` | `e3_int_min_over_zero` |\n| E4 | `div_euclid` | `v2 == 0 && v1 == INT_MAX` | returns `0` | `e4_int_max_over_zero` |\n| E5 | `div_euclid` | `v1 >= 0 && v2 == INT_MIN` — guard `v2 != (-0x7fffffff-1)` at `lib.c:11` is FALSE, so `-v2` is never evaluated; takes `q = 0, r = v1` | returns `0` (`r = v1 >= 0` ⇒ no tail adjust) | `e5_nonneg_over_int_min` |\n| E6 | `div_euclid` | `v1 < 0 && v1 != INT_MIN && v2 == INT_MIN` — guard at `lib.c:18` FALSE; takes `q = 1, r = v1 - q*v2` | returns `1` (`r = v1 - INT_MIN > 0`) | `e6_neg_over_int_min` |\n| E7 | `div_euclid` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 == INT_MIN` — guards at `lib.c:15` and `lib.c:24` both FALSE; takes `q = 1, r = 0` | returns `1` | `e7_int_min_over_int_min` |\n| E8 | `div_euclid` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 == -1` — the guarded branch at `lib.c:24-25` performs `q = ((-(v1-v2)) / (-v2)) + 1` = `INT_MAX + 1`, i.e. C signed-overflow | returns `INT_MIN` (`-2147483648`, wrapped) — must not panic | `e8_int_min_over_minus_one` |\n| E9 | `div_euclid` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 == 1` — `lib.c:22-23`, `q = -(INT_MAX/1) - 1` = `INT_MIN` (boundary of representable quotient) | returns `INT_MIN` | `e9_int_min_over_one` |\n| E10 | `div_euclid` | `v1 == INT_MIN && v2 > 0` arbitrary (randomized) — guard at `lib.c:15` FALSE, so the code must never evaluate `-v1` | same value as C, no trap | `e10_int_min_over_positive_random` |\n| E11 | `div_euclid` | `v1 == INT_MIN + 1 && v2 == -1` — guards at `lib.c:15`/`lib.c:18` both TRUE, `(-v1)/(-v2)` = `INT_MAX/1` (largest in-range result) | returns `INT_MAX` (`2147483647`) | `e11_int_min_plus_one_over_minus_one` |\n| E12 | `div_euclid` | `v1 == INT_MAX && v2 == -1` — `lib.c:11-12`, `q = -(INT_MAX/1)` | returns `-2147483647` | `e12_int_max_over_minus_one` |\n| E13 | `div_euclid` | FFI boundary: argument registers carry dirty upper 32 