lean rebuild).\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n1. **I proved the harness can fail.** I injected 15 mutations into `src/lib.rs` one at a time; 12/12 non-equivalent bugs were caught (including a single-point bug at one boundary pair). The 3 uncaught mutants are provably *equivalent*, not gaps — I confirmed empirically (temporary `assert!(a >= 0 && b > 0)` instrumentation over the whole corpus) that every `cdiv`/`crem` call site receives a non-negative dividend and positive divisor, where truncating and Euclidean division coincide. Source restored and byte-verified afterwards.\n2. **The C's one UB is not build-dependent.** `div_euclid(INT_MIN, -1)` computes `INT_MAX + 1` in C. I rebuilt the C source as gcc `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3`, `-fwrapv`, `-fno-strict-overflow`, and clang `-O2` (outputs in `target/`, never in `c_src/`); the Rust's `wrapping_add` matches **all seven** reference builds on that case and everywhere else.\n\nNo divergence was found — `src/lib.rs` required no fixes and is byte-identical to the input translation. `c_src/` is unmodified (md5s verified; only the generated `build/` directory was added, per the provided build command)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":694,"cache_read_input_tokens":115571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":694,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2e870b6-93b6-43e3-a48b-aaf583ef6a8e","uuid":"7a756e44-2c66-4fff-8091-b8d7ec3f90aa","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:02:39.636Z"}
